---
import Meta from "@/components/Meta.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <Meta
    title="Colophon"
    description="How this blog is built, from its framework to its typography."
    slot="meta"
  />
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <div class="border-ink mb-8 border-b-2 pb-6">
      <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase">
        Behind the blog
      </p>
      <h1>Colophon</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose flow max-w-2xl">
      <p>
        This is my corner of the web for software engineering and everyday
        notes. Here's what goes into making it.
      </p>
      <h2>Built with</h2>
      <p>
        The blog is built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> and
        styled with <a href="https://tailwindcss.com/">Tailwind CSS</a>. Posts
        are written in Markdown, and pages are generated as static HTML.
      </p>
      <h2>Typography</h2>
      <p>
        Text and headings use{" "}
        <a href="https://fontsource.org/fonts/nebula-sans">Nebula Sans</a>.
        Code, dates, and small labels use{" "}
        <a href="https://fontsource.org/fonts/source-code-pro">
          Source Code Pro
        </a>
        . Both fonts are self-hosted through{" "}
        <a href="https://fontsource.org/">Fontsource</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Diagrams and code</h2>
      <p>
        Diagrams are drawn with <a href="https://d2lang.com/">D2</a> and
        rendered as SVGs. Code snippets are highlighted with{" "}
        <a href="https://shiki.style/">Shiki</a> using the GitHub Light theme.
      </p>
      <h2>Follow along</h2>
      <p>
        You can <a href="/rss.xml">subscribe via RSS</a> to keep up with new
        posts. The source code is available on{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/kzuraw/blog">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</Layout>
